notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T21:55:16.402Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation (2026-11-12). Compacted strings now carry a recognisable marker: compactExplanatoryString in src/core/shared/text-normalization.ts keeps the Unicode-safe 240-code-unit prefix and appends the ellipsis plus [+N chars], where N is the omitted UTF-16 code-unit count. Both compaction walkers use it, so JSON, TOON and the context-intent path agree. readCompactionMarker recognises only a trailing marker with a positive count (tolerating trailing whitespace), so a bare ellipsis or a marker quoted mid-text is ordinary text. runAnnotationCommand in src/sdk/annotations.ts refuses an --edit whose parsed replacement ends with the marker, before taking the item lock: annotation_text_compacted, exit 2, nothing written, with details collection, entry_index and omitted_characters, and examples naming the --output-budget unbounded read and the --file edit. The guard covers comments, notes and learnings (one shared path, so CLI, SDK and MCP alike). Appends are not refused, because quoting a compacted read as evidence is legitimate. Contract change: compacted strings used to end with a bare ellipsis."
